diagnosis_text:
The failure is in the routing control-plane on switch_dist_1_1 (FRR/OSPF). The L3 SVI/subnet for Pod 1 (10.1.1.0/24) is not being advertised into OSPF from switch_dist_1_1, so the rest of the network has no route back to hosts in that subnet. Evidence: switch_dist_1_1’s FRR config only advertises 172.16.0.6/31 (uplink) in OSPF (no “network 10.1.1.0/24 area 1”), while Pod 2’s switch_dist_2_1 correctly advertises 10.2.1.0/24. Consequently, switch_server_access (10.200.0.1) lacks a route to 10.1.1.0/24 (its routing table has no such entry) and returns ICMP Destination Net Unreachable when web servers or the DNS server try to reach 10.1.1.2. We captured these unreachables coming from 10.200.0.1. From host_1_1_1_
